{
  "_about": "Mock-test blueprints. Each exam offers `tests` online mocks; every attempt generates a fresh paper in the browser from the pools listed per section (subject units / chapter ids / a bank id), avoiding questions already served on that device until the pool cycles. Chapter mocks are generated from the same chapter banks. Patterns are approximations from public sources — not official papers.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "board",
      "title": "CBSE board subjects",
      "intro": "Objective mocks modelled on the MCQ section of the board paper but stretched across the whole syllabus, so one attempt tells you which units need work. One mark per question, no negative marking."
    },
    {
      "id": "school",
      "title": "Class XI entrance tests",
      "intro": "School admission tests set on the Class X syllabus. Where an official section (General Knowledge, Indo-Islamic culture) has no question bank here, the mock says so and leaves it out."
